WEBVTT

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:05.137
In August 2024, a glacial lake above
the village of Thame, in Nepal, burst.

00:00:05.187 --> 00:00:08.942
Satellites rarely see these
lakes through monsoon cloud,

00:00:08.992 --> 00:00:11.389
but hikers walk past them every day.

00:00:11.439 --> 00:00:16.943
Lake Lookout turns a hike into a field
log, on your own laptop, with no internet.

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:19.757
In the evening, make a
day for today's hike,

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.633
and drop in the photos and
voice notes from your phone.

00:00:23.683 --> 00:00:27.600
This demo uses a test day built
from Wikimedia photos of Hunza,

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:29.351
with synthetic voice notes.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:31.584
Now press the Process button.

00:00:31.634 --> 00:00:34.086
Gemma 4 runs right here, through Ollama,

00:00:34.136 --> 00:00:39.015
and the app blocks every network connection
except the one to the local model.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:43.439
It transcribes each voice
note, and reads every photo.

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:48.874
The result is a field log:
your route, every stop,

00:00:48.924 --> 00:00:53.092
and a checklist drawn from published
glacial-lake hazard indicators.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:57.854
Every yes or no has to name its evidence:
what the model saw in the photo,

00:00:57.904 --> 00:00:59.104
or what you said.

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:02.500
Anything it can't actually
see is marked as unclear.

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:03.750
Never a silent no.

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:08.270
When the photo and your voice note
disagree, it shows both, and picks neither.

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:13.377
Answers the model couldn't back up are
downgraded, and the reason is kept.

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:16.331
Photos open full size.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:23.640
Then share one page that works offline,
plus CSV and GeoJSON for researchers.

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:26.209
And there's a dark mode for the tent.

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:27.830
Lake Lookout.

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:30.019
Open weights, no signal needed.

00:01:30.069 --> 00:01:32.209
Field observations, not alerts.

00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:36.285
Even this voice is an open
model, running on this laptop.
